meta {
  name: List Share Links
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/leads/share-links
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

tests {
  test("returns 200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("returns a plain items array", function () {
    expect(res.getBody()).to.have.property("items");
    expect(res.getBody().items).to.be.an("array");
  });

  test("every row belongs to the caller and carries a usable url", function () {
    res.getBody().items.forEach(function (row) {
      expect(row).to.have.property("url");
      expect(row).to.have.property("submissionCount");
      expect(row).to.not.have.property("producerId");
      expect(row).to.not.have.property("agencyId");
    });
  });
}

docs {
  # GET /leads/share-links — the caller's own links (PAC-37)

  Lists the links this user has minted, newest first, with their submission
  counts — enough for a producer to see which link is producing business and to
  revoke one that has leaked.

  - **Module:** `leads`
  - **Permission:** `leads:read`
  - **Data scope:** always pinned to the caller, at every scope. Even an Agency
    Owner sees only their own links here: each row contains a **working
    credential** for an unauthenticated write endpoint, so listing other
    people's is not something to do casually. A management view, if wanted, is a
    separate deliberate feature.

  Returns a plain `{ items: [...] }` array rather than the paginated envelope
  used by `GET /leads` — links per producer are a handful, and pagination here
  would be ceremony.

  ## Response `200`
  ```json
  {
    "items": [
      {
        "id": "665f0a1b2c3d4e5f60718293",
        "token": "8Kj2mQ7xR4tY9wZ1aB3cD5eF6gH8iJ0kL2mN4oP6qRs",
        "url": "http://localhost:5173/f/lead/8Kj2mQ7xR4tY9wZ1aB3cD5eF6gH8iJ0kL2mN4oP6qRs",
        "label": "Referrals from Dave at First National",
        "isActive": true,
        "submissionCount": 4,
        "lastSubmissionAt": "2026-08-02T18:31:05.000Z",
        "createdAt": "2026-07-30T09:00:00.000Z",
        "revokedAt": null
      }
    ]
  }
  ```

  Revoked links are still listed, with `isActive: false` and a `revokedAt`
  timestamp, so a producer can see what they have turned off.

  `submissionCount` counts **new leads only** — a replayed submission (a flaky
  mobile connection, a retry) does not inflate it.

  ## Errors
  - `401 Unauthorized` — missing/expired access token.
  - `403 Forbidden` — `leads` module disabled, or missing `leads:read`.
}
